<title>JAPAN: Japan May oil product imports down yr/yr--MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan May oil product imports down yr/yr--MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Trade Ministry on Tuesday issued the following data on oil product imports during May:</p>
<p>	 (In 1,000 kl) (1,000 bbl)mth/mth%  yr/yr %</p>
<p> Gasoline     202	1,271    +98.0     +46.4</p>
<p> Naphtha    2,536     15,951     +6.5	-6.4</p>
<p> Kerosene	55	  346    -40.9     -45.5</p>
<p> Gas oil	  8	   50    -84.3     -97.5</p>
<p> Fuel oil A    73	  459    -12.0     -34.8</p>
<p> Fuel oil C   296	1,862    +64.4     +19.4</p>
<p> Total	3,170     19,939     +9.7     -12.5</p>
<p>(Note: LSWR imports are included in the Fuel oil C statistics)</p>
</text>
